From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 08:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: Only load @font-face fonts that the page uses

Every @font-face rule was fetched, sanitised and kept in memory as soon as
its stylesheet applied, even when no style used its family or its
unicode-range covered no character on the page. CSS Fonts 4 requires user
agents to only download fonts that are used.

A new rule now only registers an unloaded face, matched by its descriptors.
Font matching asks for the face once it selects it for a character, and the
loads it asked for start after layout. `FontFace.load()` and
`FontFaceSet.load()` ask for faces the same way. Faces whose sources are all
`local()` are still loaded right away.

Because matching now decides which faces load, adding @font-face rules
dirties the document so that text is matched again, `document.fonts.ready`
flushes layout, and a reflow that starts loads makes it pending again.

The font store now holds templates for faces whose data has not been
downloaded. `FontGroupFamilyTemplate::font_if_matches` skips them, but
`FontContext::matching_templates` and `FontContext::font` are also used
directly by the SVG font resolver, which would hit the "Should never create
a web font without data" panic in `PlatformFont::new_from_template` for any
SVG `<text>` using a web font. `FontContext::font` returns `None` for a web
font template without data, without caching the failure, so the face can be
used once it has loaded. The SVG font resolver asks for the face to be
loaded, like layout does when it matches one, and falls back to the next
family in the meantime.

An element whose font-family names a web font but that has no text never
picks the font for a character, but its first available font is needed
too, for instance for `line-height: normal` and font-relative lengths, and
Chrome and Firefox load it. After an element is restyled, layout asks for
the first available font of its style to be loaded if it is a web font that
has not been fetched. Only elements whose font differs from their parent's
are looked at, nothing is done while the document has no web fonts, and the
lookup runs once per font group. It does not create fonts, so system fonts
are not loaded for elements that never draw text.

Testing: A new WPT test checks that unused faces stay "unloaded". A canvas
test that expected a font not used by the page to be loaded now fails, as it
does in Chrome, Firefox and Safari. svg/painting/svg-with-outline.html,
css/css-transforms/transform-box/view-box-mutation-002.html and
resize-observer/svg.html keep their expected results instead of crashing,
and content-security-policy/font-src/font-stylesheet-font-blocked.sub.html
(a body without text) and preload/preload-resource-match.https.html (an
empty paragraph) still see the font fetched.

Fork note: second of four patches, meant for upstream. The upstream-based
version (branch lazy-webfonts) does not have the two fixes for SVG text and
for elements without text yet, which the servo-ohos PR 12 try run found.
Motivation: generated-UI pages that link Google Fonts CJK families declare
hundreds of unicode-range subsets (441 @font-face rules on the "keai"
concert-article test page), and Servo downloaded all of them (437 files,
10.5 MiB) where ArkWeb downloads 64.

Relies on: the previous patch (the load state on `FontFaceRuleInfo`, which is
how matching tells unloaded faces apart and how `FontFace.status` shows it);
upstream a8d5fdaa915 (#47564, its `FontFaceSet.load` font query is what makes
`document.fonts.load()` ask for faces); matching going through
`FontGroupFamilyTemplate::font_if_matches` and `char_in_unicode_range`
(components/shared/fonts/font_template.rs); `LayoutThread::reflow` returning a
`ReflowResult` and `can_skip_reflow_request_entirely` gating it; and the
readiness checks in `Document::maybe_fulfill_font_ready_promise` and
`Window::maybe_resolve_pending_screenshot_readiness_requests` reading
`FontContext::web_fonts_still_loading`.

Drop when upstream loads @font-face rules lazily: the test this patch adds,
css/css-font-loading/fontface-unused-stays-unloaded.html, passes on plain
upstream.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 css/css-font-loading css/css-fonts html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text` (948 tests): the new fontface-unused-stays-unloaded passes; 2d.text.draw.fontface.notinpage now fails as in Chrome/Firefox/Safari; six "(drawing text in a canvas)" subtests of generic-family-keywords-003 failed with this patch on base/2026-08-29 (Chrome and Firefox pass them) and pass again since base/2026-10-08, so their expectations were dropped; the two @font-face layer-override subtests of css/css-cascade/layer-font-face-override (FAIL on plain upstream) pass with this patch, so their expectations were dropped too; matching/font-unicode-PUA subtests are intermittent (test race, both results seen); the only other unexpected result, font-variant-emoji-1 FAIL, also happens on plain ohos-main. `./mach test-wpt --release svg resize-observer css/css-transforms/transform-box` (1355 tests): all as expected (svg-with-outline, view-box-mutation-002 and resize-observer/svg crash without the SVG font resolver change). `./mach test-wpt --release css/css-fonts css/css-font-loading css/css-flexbox css/css-grid css/cssom-view css/css-inline css/css-text html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text content-security-policy/font-src preload svg` (8650 tests): no new unexpected results besides font-variant-emoji-1 and the known intermittent grid-self-alignment-fit-content-001; font-stylesheet-font-blocked.sub.html and preload-resource-match.https.html pass, and fail without the first-available-font change. Host release build, keai page served locally over HTTP/1.1 keep-alive (3 runs each): font files fetched 437 -> 66, RSS 525.3 -> 471.6 MiB, heap 340.1 -> 286.4 MiB, `--exit -o` screenshot byte-identical to ohos-main. The servo-webfont-eager-download reproducer (6 @font-face rules, 1 needed) fetches 1 font instead of 6. On a PLR-AL00, production build with `--features tracing-hitrace`, the keai page served from the host through `hdc rport`, measured with this patch and the next two applied (they change invalidation, not which fonts load): 437 -> 66 font files per load in each of 5 `servoperf page` loads, and PSS 30 s after launch 507.6 -> 467.9 MB (-7.8%, 4 interleaved loads each, every pair 35-49 MB apart).
